* WELL-BULK VARIANT (2026-08-25).  This is the bulk-ported std-cell CDL, not
* the _no_bulk one that sat here for the whole project.
* _no_bulk collapses every device bulk onto the cell's OWN VDD / VSS port.
* In a header-gated row the cell's VDD port is VDD_SW, so _no_bulk asserts
* n-well = VDD_SW -- exactly the back-feed topology hart_tile.innovus.tcl
* goes to great length to avoid (addWellTap FILLBIASA10TH, VNW->VDD).
* The layout extracts the n-well on always-on VDD, which is correct, so the
* compare produced ~61k "B: VDD vs missing connection" terminal lines per
* power net and the deck could not have seen a real well-bias defect.
* tsmc65_hvt_sc_adv10.cdl carries explicit VNW / VPW bulk ports; lvs.sh binds
* them VNW=VDD VPW=VSS on every A10TH instance, which is what
* globalNetConnect declares in the Innovus DB.
.include_cdl "/opt/design_kits/TSMC65-IP/arm/sc10/hvt/aci/sc-ad10/lvs_netlist/tsmc65_hvt_sc_adv10.cdl"
